---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Penguin-Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';

const currentDate = new Date();
let currentYear = currentDate.getFullYear();
---

<Layout title="Penguins">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
        <title>Macaroni Penguin</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <header class="header">
            <h1>Macaroni Penguin</h1>
        </header>
        <Navbar/>
        <main>
            <div class="container">
                <nav class="contents">
                    <h2>Contents:</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#diet">Diet</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#behavior">Social Behavior</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#facts">Facts</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

                <section id="overview">
                    <h2>Overview</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Scientific Name: Eudyptes chrysolophus</li>
                        <li>Size: Approximately 70 cm (28 inches) tall, weighing 3-7 kg (6.6-15.4 lbs).</li>
                        <li>Habitat: Found in the subantarctic and Antarctic Peninsula regions, with major breeding colonies on South Georgia, South Sandwich Islands, and the Falkland Islands.</li>
                        <li>Conservation Status: Vulnerable</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <section id="diet">
                    <h2>Diet</h2>
                    <p>The Macaroni Penguin's diet consists primarily of krill, as well as other crustaceans, small fish, and squid, which they forage for in the Southern Ocean.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="behavior">
                    <h2>Social Behavior</h2>
                    <p>Macaroni Penguins are highly social and breed in very large and dense colonies, sometimes numbering in the hundreds of thousands. They are known for their loud vocalizations and active social interactions, especially during the breeding season when they establish territories and pair bonds. They often exhibit aggressive behavior towards neighbors.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="facts">
                    <h2>Interesting Facts</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>They are easily identified by their striking orange-yellow crest that extends from their forehead.</li>
                        <li>Macaroni Penguins undertake long migrations outside of the breeding season.</li>
                        <li>Similar to Erect-Crested Penguins, they lay two eggs, with the first egg being significantly smaller and usually not surviving.</li>
                        <li>Their large colony sizes can create significant disturbance to the breeding grounds.</li>
                        <li>Populations have declined in recent decades, likely due to factors such as climate change and changes in prey availability.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
            <footer>
                <p><span class="copyleft">&copy;</span> PengiCoder & MrPiggy105, { currentYear }</p>
            </footer>
        </main>
    </body>
</Layout>

<style>
    .contents ul {
        list-style-type: none;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .contents li {
        margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    section {
        overflow: hidden;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        margin-left: 30%;
    }

    h1{
        text-align: center;
        height: 100%;
        font-family: 'Orkney', Arial;
    }
</style>